  "source_cause": "During InitCommand conversions.lua calls GetTopScreen. The capture returns nil, while the independent scene returns ScreenGameplay and adds a GetName query. Pinned ScreenManager.cpp:342 returns null when the screen stack is empty; its Lua binding returns nil for that state.",
  "change": "Production gameplay context marks screen loading. The compiler retains the owned screen and actor parents while GetTopScreen returns nil during construction/Init. It exposes the screen immediately before Begin, matching PushLoadedScreen. The same scope is set for each replacement scene. Standalone active-host actor compilation keeps its active screen, and End still sees the popped screen.",
